preConditionHook:
// THE MICRO CHANNEL ENDS, SO THE WITH-TREND TRADE ENDS. A long taken inside a
// bull micro channel is closed by the first bar that violates the run of higher
// lows: the channel must have held over the minBars bar pairs ENDING AT BAR 1,
// and this bar makes a strictly lower low. Short is the mirror on highs.
//
// Same run test as MicroChannelRunLength read one bar back, so the loop runs
// i = 1..minBars and reaches low[minBars + 1]. Containment is INCLUSIVE -- an
// equal low keeps a bull micro channel alive -- so only a strictly lower low
// breaks it, and the relationals carry the 2.22e-12 tolerance via el_lt/el_gt.
//
// The condition text is MicroChannelBreakoutBar's plus a position guard, in the
// EXIT role. That pairing is established here (ConsecutiveCloseExit is
// MomentumConsecutiveBars in the exit pane; AdverseBodyCountExit is
// ConsecutiveUpBars mirrored there) and an Entry rule cannot occupy the exit
// pane. Unlike AdverseBodyCountExit this one DOES read position state, because
// the side matters: the bull channel is what takes the long off.
//
// Same shape as ExitOnFirstOppositeBodyAfterRun but the run is counted on higher
// lows rather than on bull bodies, so the two fire on different bars.
priorChanLow = true;
priorChanHigh = true;
for (int i = 1; i <= (int)minBars; ++i) {
    if (el_lt(low[i], low[i + 1])) priorChanLow = false;
    if (el_gt(high[i], high[i + 1])) priorChanHigh = false;
}
